From f65324bcbd00cd05781326bea84cecb9e68e669f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arnaldo Lima <arnaldolimaof@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:40:43 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Files past 2 GB, and _cellSpursLFQueuePushBody

cellFs: lseek, fstat and stat kept positions and sizes in long and struct
stat, 32 bits on Windows: God of War: Ascension's RESOURCES.PSARC (2.1 GB)
could not be mounted and its init failed. They go through 64-bit helpers
now (_fseeki64/_ftelli64/_stat64; fseeko/ftello elsewhere). All 19 of the
game's archives mount, the 9 GB one included.

_cellSpursLFQueuePushBody: the producer half of the ring
cellSpursQueuePushBody models (W0 pop, W1 push, modulo 2*W3), written under
the lock-line lock with raw accesses (the vm_ accessors take that lock),
then the task parked on the queue's line is woken
(spu_signal_parked_on_line, as an LFQueue made on the SPURS names no
taskset). The game's first SPU task now takes its first message.
SPURS_LFQUEUE_NO_PUSH=1 makes it a no-op again.
---
